{"abstract":[{"text":"The types every other module shares: the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Event"},{"text":" protocol, the values its properties can hold, and the record a tracker makes of each event.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An event is a value that conforms to "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Event","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", declared with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"type":"text","text":". Its stored properties"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are its properties, so a misspelled or mistyped one is a compile error. Its type gives the name"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"destinations record it under, the "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/ConsentCategory","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" whose consent decides whether it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delivered, and the version of its shape. Each has a default: the type’s name,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/ConsentCategory\/analytics","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" and 1."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Two property types carry rules of their own. A ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Sensitive","type":"reference"},{"text":" value, such as an email address,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"prints as ","type":"text"},{"code":"<redacted>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and has no public accessor: a destination reads it through","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/EventRecord\/reveal(_:)","type":"reference"},{"text":